WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.580
SSO and MFA require ongoing monitoring after deployment.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:21.320
Authentication logs, sign-in events, failed login patterns, MFA enrollment changes, MFA reset events, suspicious approval behavior, privileged account activity, token anomalies, application consent events, and policy changes all tell part of the identity story.

3
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.860
Without monitoring, a centralized identity system can become a centralized blind spot.

4
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.780
Alerting should focus on meaningful signals.

5
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:44.280
Repeated failures, impossible-travel-style patterns, unusual enrollment changes, unexpected privileged sign-ins, new application consent, policy exceptions, and high-risk session behavior may deserve review.

6
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.580
The goal is not to generate noise for every login.

7
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:56.160
The goal is to detect changes that could indicate account compromise, misconfiguration, risky access, or operational drift.

8
00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.760
Incident response plans should include identity-specific actions.

9
00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:13.020
Teams may need to disable accounts, revoke sessions, reset authenticators, rotate keys or certificates, review application assignments, inspect consent grants, and preserve logs.

10
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:19.520
Recovery should be coordinated so the organization restores safe access without destroying evidence or creating new gaps.

11
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:24.420
Help desk and operations teams should know when identity events require escalation.

12
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.420
Governance keeps the system aligned over time.

13
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:34.000
Access reviews confirm that users, groups, privileged roles, and application assignments still make sense.

14
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.780
Policy exceptions should be owned and time-bound.

15
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.120
Audit trails should show who changed identity settings and why.

16
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:51.580
SSO and MFA are powerful controls, but their value depends on review, ownership, monitoring, and the willingness to correct drift.
